<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Defs>

  <!-- Animal Apparel: Framework defines exactly three groups for animals - AnimalHead,
       AnimalBody and AnimalLegs - and its Bodies.xml puts the Neck part into AnimalBody,
       because Neck is neither a head nor a leg. A collar therefore has nowhere of its own
       to sit: it lands in the same group as the flak jacket and the plate armour.

       AnimalNeck is a fourth group, filled by Patches/Bodies_AnimalNeck.xml. It is what
       makes a collar a separate garment rather than a competitor for the body slot:
       RimWorld refuses to wear two items together only when they share BOTH a body part
       group and a layer, so a collar on AnimalNeck never conflicts with anything on
       AnimalBody, whatever layer either of them uses.

       Draw order is a different question and is not solved here. The framework gives every
       piece of animal apparel the same baseLayer (70, from the single AnimalApparel render
       tag), so items would otherwise stack in whatever order the animal happens to wear
       them. Each collar sets <apparel><drawData><defaultData><layer> to override it - see
       the comment on the collar defs.

       listOrder 98 keeps it inside the framework's own block (AnimalHead 99, AnimalBody
       100, AnimalLegs 101). That block is already inverted with respect to vanilla, where
       higher means higher up the body; the value only affects the order parts are listed
       in the coverage tooltip. -->
  <BodyPartGroupDef>
    <defName>AnimalNeck</defName>
    <label>neck</label>
    <listOrder>98</listOrder>
  </BodyPartGroupDef>

</Defs>
